    <!-- ALWAYS ON despite the warn default: the tests' OWN narration, not the product's. What made the
         default noisy is product logging (one ParallelConsumerOptions toString per construction, the
         control loop); a test that deliberately logs a line is saying something worth reading. Above all
         the chaos suite's run-start banner - "=== CHAOS W1 churn storm: seed=... (replay: ...) ===" - which
         is the only copy of the seed on a PASSING run; buildAutopsy() reprints it on failure, but a pass
         that you later want to replay has nothing else. Integration tests have no resources dir of their
         own, so failsafe reads THIS file. -->
    <!-- Same knob, floor of info rather than warn: a hard "info" here would make
         -Dpc.log.level=debug silently NOT raise the integration tests, which is the case you most
         want it for. -->
    <logger name="bz.stub.parallelconsumer.integrationTests" level="${pc.log.level:-info}"/>

    <!-- ALWAYS ON despite the warn default: adaptive concurrency's target trajectory. The controller is the
         one component whose entire observable product is a handful of lines - it speaks only when the admission
         target MOVES (at most one line per one-second window, and most windows hold) or, rate-limited to one
         line per five seconds, when a named constraint is holding the target still. The feature is opt-in and
         off by default, so on every other test in the suite this logger emits nothing at all; on
         AdaptiveConcurrencyEnforceIT it is the whole point of the run, and it is what makes
         `-Dit.test=AdaptiveConcurrencyEnforceIT` watchable without also enabling -Dpc.log.level=debug, which
         would bury it. Both lines open with "Adaptive concurrency" - see AdmissionController's javadoc. -->
    <logger name="bz.stub.parallelconsumer.internal.admission.AdmissionController" level="info"/>

